## 1. What was added

main.py, run_live_mode(): after the graph is restored (or reset) and before the
`you> ` loop, when --observe is given:

  from .visualiser.tap import observe as start_observation
  observer = start_observation(runtime, journal_path=observe_journal,
                               interval=0.2, source_note="main.py live")
  print("[machine] Observing to " + observer.journal_path, flush=True)

The import is inside the branch, so a normal live session never loads the
visualiser package. Two flags were added to the parser:

  $ PYTHONPATH=/home/user python cat_theo_machine/main.py live --help
    --observe             For live mode, also write the graph changes to the
                          visualiser's observation journal.
    --observe-journal OBSERVE_JOURNAL
                          Journal file for --observe (default: the visualiser's
                          run/observed.jsonl).

visualiser/events.py, GraphDigest._rules_chain(): the runtime's compiled rule
list is used when it is a pair; when it is not (live mode loads packs straight
into the graph through PackLoader, which never fills the runtime's compiled
list) the graph's own rule order is read instead. Measured on the live path:

  PackLoader.load_pack_file(path, runtime.graph)
    runtime.ordered_rules()            -> not a pair (empty)
    M.FromContextGetRuleOrder(graph)() -> 12 rules
  GraphDigest(...).read()              -> 12 rule edges, counts.rule_total 12

The same fallback also covers a restored graph on which the compiled list
raises AttributeError ('Atom' object has no attribute 'inputs'); see section 5.

